{"kind":"assert","text":"J2 acceptance, step 1: versions 1 and 2 ran on the real room, and Artifacts served every read. Version 3 needs you to move the base. The acceptance is not met.\n\nThe run: `apps/views/src/node.ts` over stdio with a scripted MCP client, under the enrolled home agent-a, against dap-demo version f171fce3, source 8851f19d. Change 2, \"Describe the task list in the README\", lane sc_todnomcob4zewgp35xrn4sqj4lv6cz73hgsuf4eapawwhil734ma, one sentence in README.md. Version 1 is 49eea438 on base aeae3275, manifest entry 21. Version 2 is c296c980 on the same base, manifest entry 29. Evidence: ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-j2-acceptance/, SHA256SUMS d7a4e943b1dda8447707b1eb1091f702a89fdb27c408cfa92ac136e96df19321, read-only.\n\nObserved on the deployed Worker:\n- Each view's band equals the answer's commits and `git rev-parse`. Diff, interdiff and file, on both versions.\n- Each new read signs one read-token act, at destination entries 22 to 30. A held read and reading the card sign nothing.\n- The largest view_act answer is 15,832 bytes on the wire, the interdiff.\n- No answer holds the read-session bearer, a workspace token or the provider token's shape. A byte search of the 110 evidence files finds none.\n\nThe page's words come from a replay in Chromium with the real bundle and the recorded answers. That is a proxy for the app.\n\nWhat differs from the note and your brief:\n1. Artifacts did not refuse, and the staged commits are advertised. `git ls-remote` with a fresh read token lists each one under refs/artroom/staged/. So any read token lists all 3 staged refs in the room, and any member holding one can fetch unmerged work. Please say whether that is the rule you want. I change nothing.\n2. One shallow fetch failed: `--depth=1` of version 1 on protocol 0 said \"expected shallow list\". The views do not use a shallow fetch.\n3. The answer is larger than the note says. A frame holds the text six times, escaped, not twice. By reconstruction, not a run, a frame reaches about 175 KiB at 40 KiB of text and about 198 KiB at about 30 KiB of text. So a person on this change witnesses about 16 KB only. I will file a small head that cuts the copies, because a result that repeats itself serves no reader. A person does not need to wait for it.\n4. A review of version 1 is no longer possible, because `review-verdict` requires a current manifest. The person's Request changes goes on version 2.\n5. The note's configuration entry exits 127 with a minimal PATH. The person's steps name /opt/homebrew/bin/node.\n\nWhat needs you:\n1. **Move the base.** Agents cannot land a change: only @owner holds change.merge, and the rules need one approval. agent-a authors a second small change now, on another file, and stops at its manifest. I tell you its lane. You sign `review-verdict` and `merge` with the owner's home, because I do not use that home. Then I rebase, stage and propose version 3 with `previous` 29, with an edit of its own.\n2. **A person's time.** The steps are in person-steps.md in the evidence unit. They use the home `owner`, because @owner is the only person in the room, and nobody has started the entry under that home. They sign permanent read-token acts and one Request changes as @owner. Please decide whether @owner is the right reviewer or whether the owner enrols a person with role `member`, which holds change.review and not change.merge. You ask for that time when you choose. Version 3 needs a second session unless the person waits for it, so I suggest asking after version 3 exists.\n\nKeep .builder-worktrees/j2-accept-20261101 out of the sweep: the person's entry runs from it. Dap-demo deployments stay on hold until I say the run has finished, because the views read from it. The checker's review of step 1 comes with the note on a head when version 3 has run.","body":{"request":"2082efd92c58b0ab84fa77fb4f3660c1722b3e4a"}}